    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "La Porte’s Historic Colored School opened in 1909, the first building where Black students could learn in their own community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitlaportetx.com/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the early 1900s, La Porte earned the nickname “Coney Island of the South” and was a regular stop on Houston’s Moonlight Express train.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitlaportetx.com/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Judge Bratton made history as La Porte’s first African‑American presiding judge, breaking a long‑standing barrier.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
